# Keep host artifacts out of the image build context (infra/web.Dockerfile
# does COPY . . from the repo root and installs/builds fresh inside the image).
#
# This context does not stay on the machine: `pnpm deploy:*` builds through
# Fly's REMOTE builder, so everything not excluded here is uploaded. Anything
# the in-container build does not need should be listed, both because uploading
# it is slow and because it leaves the machine.
node_modules
**/node_modules
# Local agent state, and in particular `.claude/worktrees`: full checkouts of
# other branches (5.4 GB across 5 worktrees on one developer's machine). The
# node_modules/.next rules below already stripped most of that bulk, so the
# measured cost was 41.5 MB of context vs 8.9 MB without it - roughly 33 MB of
# other branches' source uploaded to the remote builder on every deploy.
# Smaller than it first looks, and still nothing the build has any use for.
.claude
**/.claude
.cursor
**/.cursor
.pnpm-store
# Build output, at the repo root and in every workspace package. Without the
# `**/` globs a locally-built apps/web/.next (500MB+) gets shipped in the build
# context, since a bare `.next` only matches the root. The image builds fresh
# inside the container, so none of this is needed.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
.turbo
**/.turbo
# Playwright / test artifacts from local runs.
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
e2e/.tmp
**/e2e/.tmp
# tsc -b incremental markers, at every level. A stale nested tsbuildinfo makes
# `tsc -b` skip a package build (so its dist is never produced) while the dist
# itself is excluded above, breaking the in-container build. Excluding both
# forces a clean rebuild, matching CI.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.env
.env.*
.git
.github
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
